---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import WhatsAppFab from '../components/WhatsAppFab.astro';

const lastUpdated = "17 April 2026";
---
<Layout title="Terms of Service — CJMuse IT Support" description="The terms under which CJMuse IT Support provides services to clients.">
  <Header />

  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>These terms set out the agreement between CJMuse IT Support ("CJMuse", "I", "my") and you, the client ("you", "your"), when I provide services to you. They're written in plain English because that's the whole point. By engaging me for any service, you agree to these terms.</p>

    <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      CJMuse IT Support is operated by Sam Carew (trading as CJMuse IT Support), 1, Suite Ra01, 195-197 Wood Street, London, E17 3NU, United Kingdom.
      Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@cjmuse.com">hello@cjmuse.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Services</h2>
    <p>I provide IT services to small and solo businesses, including (but not limited to):</p>
    <ul>
      <li>General technical support and troubleshooting</li>
      <li>Email and domain setup</li>
      <li>Device security, virus removal and backups</li>
      <li>Website design and build</li>
      <li>Microsoft 365 backup and administration</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The specific scope of what I'll do for you is agreed in writing (email is fine) before work starts.</p>

    <h2>3. Quotes and pricing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Quotes are valid for <strong>30 days</strong> from the date given unless I state otherwise.</li>
      <li>Quotes are based on the information you provide. If the scope changes once I'm working, I'll tell you in writing before doing the extra work — you won't get surprise bills.</li>
      <li>All prices are in pounds sterling (GBP). CJMuse IT Support is not currently VAT-registered, so no VAT is charged.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Payment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>For one-off work, invoices are issued on completion and payable within <strong>14 days</strong>.</li>
      <li>For projects over £750, I may ask for a deposit (typically 30–50%) before work starts.</li>
      <li>Ongoing support and monthly retainers are billed in advance.</li>
      <li>Late payment may incur interest at the statutory rate under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998.</li>
      <li>Preferred payment method: bank transfer to the details on the invoice.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. What you agree to</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Give me accurate information so I can do the job properly.</li>
      <li>Give me reasonable access to the devices, accounts, or systems I need to work on (remote or in person, as agreed).</li>
      <li>Back up your own data before I work on anything, or ask me to take a backup first — see section 7.</li>
      <li>Confirm you own (or have permission to use) any content, logos, images or material you give me for website work.</li>
      <li>Pay invoices on time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Turnaround and timescales</h2>
    <p>I aim to respond to enquiries within a few business hours. Actual turnaround depends on the job and my current workload. Any timeline I quote is a best-faith estimate unless explicitly agreed in writing as a deadline.</p>

    <h2>7. Data, backups and loss</h2>
    <p>I'll take reasonable care with your devices, accounts and data. That said:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>IT work sometimes carries a risk of data loss. Where possible I'll back up before making changes — but you remain ultimately responsible for ensuring you have your own backups of anything important.</li>
      <li>I can set up backup systems for you as part of the service, but you're responsible for checking they're running and restoring from them if you need to.</li>
      <li>I am not liable for loss of data, revenue or opportunity caused by third-party services (Microsoft, Google, your internet provider, hosting providers, etc.) that are outside my control.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Many services I deliver rely on third parties — Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, domain registrars, web hosts, and others. Their terms, uptime and pricing are outside my control and may change. I'll flag anything material that affects you.</p>

    <h2>9. Website projects — intellectual property</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your content</strong> (text, images, logos you supply) remains yours.</li>
      <li><strong>The finished website</strong> — its code, design and content — transfers to you on <strong>full payment</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>My tools, templates, code libraries and know-how</strong> stay mine. You get a licence to use them as part of your website, but you don't own them and can't resell them separately.</li>
      <li>Third-party assets (stock images, open-source libraries, fonts, plugins) remain licensed by their owners on their own terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. Cancellation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Either of us can cancel an ongoing arrangement with <strong>14 days' written notice</strong> (email is fine).</li>
      <li>For project work already in progress, you pay for work completed up to the point of cancellation.</li>
      <li>If I need to cancel (for example, if I can't deliver the work), I'll refund any advance payment for work not yet done.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>Anything you tell me about your business, systems or clients is confidential. I won't share it with anyone outside of my suppliers (see the privacy policy) without your permission, unless required by law.</p>

    <h2>12. Liability</h2>
    <p>Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything that cannot be excluded under UK law.</p>
    <p>Subject to that, my total liability to you for any claim relating to the services is capped at the total fees you have paid me in the <strong>12 months</strong> before the claim arose.</p>
    <p>I'm not liable for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Indirect, consequential or loss-of-profit claims</li>
      <li>Issues caused by third-party services outside my control</li>
      <li>Issues caused by changes you, your staff, or a third party make to systems I've set up, without telling me</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>13. Privacy</h2>
    <p>How I handle personal data is covered in my <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>I may update these terms occasionally. The version in force for your work is the one posted when you accepted the quote. Material changes for ongoing arrangements will be communicated in advance.</p>

    <h2>15. Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales. Any disputes are subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the English courts.</p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:hello@cjmuse.com">hello@cjmuse.com</a>.</p>
  </article>

  <Footer />
  <WhatsAppFab />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose{
    max-width:720px;
    padding-top:40px;
    padding-bottom:72px;
    color:#2c2c2c;
  }
  .prose h1{font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,42px);margin-bottom:8px}
  .prose h2{font-size:22px;margin-top:40px;margin-bottom:12px}
  .prose p, .prose li{font-size:16px;line-height:1.7}
  .prose ul{padding-left:22px;margin:0 0 16px}
  .prose li{margin-bottom:8px}
  .prose a{color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--gold);text-underline-offset:3px}
  .prose a:hover{color:var(--gold-dark)}
  .prose .meta{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-bottom:32px}
  .prose .back{margin-bottom:24px}
  .prose .back a{color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;font-size:14px}
  .prose .back a:hover{color:var(--navy)}
  .prose strong{color:var(--navy)}
</style>
